    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I fixed `mock_openai()` in `tests/fakes.py`, and both digest tests pass again (`pytest -q`: 2 passed).\n\n**Why it broke:** openai 3.19.2 sends its requests through `httpx2`, a separate package from `httpx`. respx only patches `httpx`, so it never saw the SDK's requests. The mock was still active; it just wasn't watching the client doing the sending, so there was no warning.\n\n**The fix:** instead of respx, the helper now replaces the send method (`SyncAPIClient._send_request`) on the class that every synchronous OpenAI client inherits from, for the length of the `with` block. Because the change is on the class, it reaches every client, including app.digest's cached one and clients made before the block. The helper's interface and the canned replies are the same as before.\n\n- **Loud failure if the SDK changes:** the patch uses `autospec=True`, so if a future openai release renames or changes that method, the helper raises an error instead of quietly doing nothing.\n- **Unexpected requests:** a request other than `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions` raises an `AssertionError` instead of going to the network, much as respx did for requests it had no route for.\n- **Trade-off:** `_send_request` is a private SDK method. I chose it because respx has no `httpx2` support and it's the one point every sync client sends through.\n- `respx` is no longer imported by `tests/fakes.py`. I left it in `pyproject.toml` as you asked.\n\nI also checked the other promises in the docstring with a scratch script:\n- a client created before the block and one created inside it both got the canned replies;\n- a request after the replies ran out got a 400 error;\n- all three requests were recorded;\n- the original method was back in place after the block.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** that scratch file, `scratch_check.py`, is still in the project root because deleting it needs your approval. Please delete it yourself.\n\nThe helper's docstring says it's copied into the ops-bot repo, so that copy will n"
